# AMI replay manifest — dev split, 18 meetings.
#
# One line per meeting: ORDER  MEETING  FLAGS  SPEAKERS
#
# SPEAKERS are AMI global participant IDs, read from the RTTM speaker field.
# No new metadata: the corpus already says who is in the room, and the same
# ID in two meetings is the same person. The harness re-reads them from the
# corpus and refuses to run if this file disagrees, so the manifest is
# checked against the corpus rather than trusted.
#
# ORDER is the sequence the replay feeds meetings to one store, and it is
# what makes somebody a returner. **Order within a series' a-d suffix is
# known. Order across series, and within IB, is declared, not known** —
# AMI publishes no recording chronology for them. Any report from this
# manifest has to say so.
#
# FLAGS:
#   .                  nothing special
#   unscorable-returns the returning events in this meeting do not score.
#                      IB4001 and IB4002 hold the same four people, and their
#                      labels are permuted between the two — a different-label
#                      nearest neighbour above 0.8 for all four can only be the
#                      partner meeting, and only FIE038 is shared any further,
#                      so nothing model-free says which of the pair is wrong.
#                      Both stay in the chronology, in DER and as open-set
#                      probes; only the four returning events stop scoring.
#                      FIE038's later returns are reported on their own line,
#                      tagged as carrying a history that includes this pair.
 1  ES2011a   .                   FEE041 FEE042 FEE043 FEE044
 2  ES2011b   .                   FEE041 FEE042 FEE043 FEE044
 3  ES2011c   .                   FEE041 FEE042 FEE043 FEE044
 4  ES2011d   .                   FEE041 FEE042 FEE043 FEE044
 5  IB4001    .                   FIE038 FIO093 MIO091 MIO092
 6  IB4002    unscorable-returns  FIE038 FIO093 MIO091 MIO092
 7  IB4003    .                   FIE037 MIO036 MIO039 MIO094
 8  IB4004    .                   FIE037 MIO036 MIO039 MIO094
 9  IB4010    .                   FIE038 MIO036 MIO046 MIO095
